WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.300
- Conal Cochran, the owner
of the widely popular

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.910
Silver Shamrock Novelties Halloween

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.930
mask manufacturing company in 1982,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.960
may have been born some
time around the 10th century

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.940
in Celtic Ireland.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.320
While it is never made exactly clear

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.560
just how old Cochran is,
what is clear is that,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.740
while he appears on the surface

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.790
to be a successful
60-something entrepreneur

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.120
who essentially runs the small town

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.360
of Santa Mira, California,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.240
he is actually a sinister child murderer.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.810
Cochran comes up with a devious plan

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:23.920
to sell hundreds of thousands

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.350
of rubber Halloween masks to children,

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.210
embedded with a chip
that will eventually kill

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.550
whoever is wearing it.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.960
This is where I would say
that a plan to attack citizens

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.540
with microchips is a great plan
for a sci-fi horror premise,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.780
because nobody would be dumb enough

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.040
to think that would actually happen,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.547
but here we (piano tone) are.

00:00:37.547 --> 00:00:39.009
(ominous music)

00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:40.570
(man screaming)

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.760
He reveals himself to be
a studier of witchcraft,

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.870
intending to sacrifice as
many children as possible,

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.160
during the Festival of Samhain,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.390
a holiday which eventually
became known in our culture

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.223
as Halloween.

00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:51.520
Although in my culture,
that's just everyday.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.030
To learn more about Conal Cochran,

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.330
and why he wants to sacrifice

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.640
hundreds of thousands of children

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.480
and if he can ever actually die,

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.575
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:02.658
(ominous rock music)

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.870
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.710
I've never met anyone named
Conal in my entire life.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.290
The Halloween franchise has endured

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.650
over the last six decades,

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.390
thanks mostly in part to the popularity

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.690
of it's main antagonist.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:16.730
Maybe you've heard of him.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.280
But there is another
antagonist that I find just as,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.570
if not more fascinating.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.500
And I'm not talking about
Dr. Loomis circa 1989.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.140
- What about your stepmother, Jamie?

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.700
- His initial roots could
date back thousands of years.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.650
Cochran expresses
frustration with the fact

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.430
that most people today celebrate Halloween

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.480
without really understanding its origins.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.013
- You don't really know
much about Halloween.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.130
You thought no further
than the strange custom

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:44.967
of having your children wear masks

00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:47.290
and go out begging for candy.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.820
- He describes a time over 3000 years ago,

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.320
in what he refers to
as his old celtic lands

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.900
where the barriers would be down between

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.200
what he describes as
the real and the unreal.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.030
He explains that this
was a time where the dead

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.060
could look in on the living,

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.010
referred to as the Festival of Samhain.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.490
He explains that in the festival

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.880
they would have to make
human and animal sacrifices,

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.880
saying that the hills
ran red with the blood

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:07.990
of animals and children.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.120
To completely understand
Cochran's motivation

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.900
for wanting to sacrifice an
entire generation of children,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.540
we must take it back to the original

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.494
Pagan Festival of Samhain.

00:02:16.494 --> 00:02:19.494
(suspenseful music)

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.610
The Festival of Samhain took
place around the 10th century,

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.059
and was one of four fire festival.

00:02:26.059 --> 00:02:28.720
(upbeat music)

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.360
Not that kind of Fyre Festival.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.680
That deserves it's own
episode of Horror History.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.580
Samhain was considered

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.300
to be the most significant fire festival,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.320
meant to usher in the
winter season's harvest.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.090
It would take place
between the fall equinox

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.090
and the winter solstice,

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.950
which would fall from
the night of October 31st

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.630
through the morning of November 1st.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.680
Hearth fires in family
homes were set to burn out

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.870
while the harvest was gathered.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.970
The Samhain Festival was,
indeed, believed to be

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.820
a connection between the
living and the spirits

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.230
of those who had passed, where
a barrier would come down.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.170
There was a fear that this
barrier could be breachable

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.930
by fairies, or other evil creatures

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.540
that could get through and inflict harm.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.660
It was believed that the best way

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.830
to deflect these evil spirits

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.340
was by putting an offering
outside of individual homes.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.940
While the offerings usually consisted

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:05.900
of parts of the harvest,

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.810
sometimes they would also include cattle.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.350
If Cochran was around for the
original Samhain Festivals

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.610
then he would have been very familiar

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.440
with the practice of
putting out sacrifices

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.080
to ward off monsters and fairies.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.270
However, the belief system

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.740
that Cochran subscribes
to gets much more specific

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.790
and instead of offering
crops or livestock,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.060
involves the sacrifice of human children.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.730
It seems maybe Cochran just
really doesn't like kids.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.560
- I do love a good joke.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.020
And this is the best ever,
a joke on the children.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.210
- Yes, by killing them.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.070
Cochran explains that
the last big festival

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.600
happened 3000 years ago.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.840
When he describes it, he's
speaking in the first person,

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.580
suggesting that he was either there,

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.480
or he's just speaking
on behalf of his people.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.110
- It was the start of the
year in our old celtic lands

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:49.950
and we'd be waiting in our
houses of wattles and clay.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.040
- So, if that was the last
big festival and he was there,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.480
then what was he doing
over the next 3000 years?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.270
While Cochran's activity
from these festivals

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.640
up until the 20th century
is not completely clear,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.240
we do know what he accomplished
within the last 300.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.010
At some point, Cochran
established a company

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.790
known as Silver Shamrock Novelties.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:06.623
I'm guessing the company

00:04:06.623 --> 00:04:08.610
probably started in his
home country of Ireland,

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.490
then at some point moved
to Munich, Germany,

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:11.750
which he describes to be the birthplace

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.320
of this old woman knitting animatronic,

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.470
which was developed in 1785.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.170
Silver Shamrock sold novelties.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.350
These are usually gift items

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.670
that may appeal to someone
without having much, if any,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:21.800
practical purpose.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.570
He showcases some of his best creations

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.120
in what he calls The Hall of Fame.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.010
Many of the toys that are
featured in the background

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.390
look like they may have been
made in the early 1900s.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.920
Many of them are the kind that wind up

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.490
or require some kind of inner mechanics

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.380
to move and function.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.330
Cochran is also said to be truly famous

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.950
for his practical jokes
or prank toys and items.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.740
He's referred to as the all time genius

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.202
of the practical joke.

00:04:41.202 --> 00:04:43.696
- He invented sticky toilet paper.

00:04:43.696 --> 00:04:44.529
- Oh.

00:04:44.529 --> 00:04:45.610
- Oh you must know.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.190
The dead dwarf guy, the soft chain saw.

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.300
All his!

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.480
- From early on, it's obvious

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.650
that Cochran's target
demographic is children,

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.250
and he would shift his
focus over the years

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.370
to cater to whatever
was popular with kids.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.780
But his interest in producing toys

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.003
had more than one ulterior motive.

00:05:00.003 --> 00:05:03.003
(suspenseful music)

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.050
Being a producer of wind-up toys early on

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.710
allowed him to learn the engineering skill

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.750
to make his figures
move and seem life-like.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.320
And with 100s of years of
practice, he mastered the art,

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.660
and became known for making the most

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.350
realistic looking masks on the market,

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.990
which is part of why they're so popular.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.160
Put these two skills together,

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.510
and it becomes very easy
to see why Cochran's plans

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.030
and schemes are so threatening.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.220
Cochran's factory workers,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.400
as well as most citizens
in the town of Santa Mira,

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.230
seem to be under his complete control.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.960
His men seem to have an almost
robotic level of obedience

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.010
towards him, but what
outsiders don't realize

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:40.180
is that this is because robotic
is exactly what they are.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.270
Cochran set up an entire town of robots

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.470
to do all of his bidding,
both for his business,

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.060
his town, and for his
overall sacrificial plan.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.510
Because of the fact that he
spent, likely, hundreds of years

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.850
developing the mechanisms for
his toys and figures to move,

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.600
he was able apply all of that knowledge

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.700
towards creating an entire town of robots.

00:05:58.242 --> 00:06:00.670
- The surprising thing is
that the internal components

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.027
were quite simple to produce, really.

00:06:03.027 --> 00:06:05.840
The outer features took
much longer to perfect

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:06.870
but then of course in the end,

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.810
it's just another form of mask making.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.590
- The business arrived
at the small farming town

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:14.030
of Santa Mira, California
in 1945, after World War II.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.210
It's no mistake that Cochran
chose to build his factory

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.560
far away from civilization,

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.350
where he could still launch
a successful business

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.810
but without a large population

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.750
being able to see exactly
what he was doing.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.090
By then Cochran was already
described as being wealthy,

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.560
which means that he likely
already had a successful business

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.450
by this point.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.850
The entire city is placed
under constant surveillance

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.760
and is locked down with
a six o'clock curfew,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.510
allowing Cochran to do whatever he wants

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.610
under the cover of nightfall,

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.370
without having to worry
about the prying eyes

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.150
of the townspeople seeing what he's up to.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.260
But how was Conal Cochran

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.460
able to keep himself alive for so long?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.930
As he explains the history
of The Festival of Samhain,

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.260
he confirms that he
harnesses what most outsiders

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.860
would refer to as witchcraft,

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.720
but he simply sees it as a form of alchemy

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.600
that his people use to control the world.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.400
This would actually make
sense, especially in 1982.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.860
In the early 1980s, modern
Pagans known as Wiccans

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.200
started a revival of Samhain,

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.210
which was a ceremony
involving music and dance

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.410
called Witches' Balls.

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:03.840
A very not good title,

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.920
but at least they didn't
call them Cochran Balls.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.910
However, in real life,
sacrificing children

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.190
was not part of the festival.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.230
That's a pretty specific Cochran thing.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.530
Maybe he was bullied by some
kids one time or something.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.080
By 1982, the main focus of Silver Shamrock

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.630
was selling Halloween masks for kids,

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.360
but again, the masks were only
part of a much larger plan.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.560
His real goal was to get
the kids wearing their masks

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.860
in front of a television screen,

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.240
where a hypnotic advertisement

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:26.850
would trigger a particle within the masks

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.310
and a beam would turn the kids' heads

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.350
into a series of bugs and snakes.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.410
Making a TV program the center of his plan

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.910
fits in with what Cochran
has basically done all along:

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.430
follow the interests of the youth.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.270
The 1980s were the
beginning of a golden age

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.770
for kids television programming.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.390
Youth pop culture was driven by things

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.490
like Teenage Mutant Ninja
Turtles and Transformers,

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.230
whose popularity revolved around cartoons

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.250
airing at the time.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.850
Cochran has to commit
this sacrifice in 1982

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.280
due to the alignment of the planets

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.440
during that year's festival.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.770
To pull this off, he
needs a magical artifact,

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.850
a monolith from the famous
prehistoric monument Stonehenge.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.480
This is because each part of Stonehenge

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.030
is meant to represent one of
the 19 cycles of the moon.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.650
Basically, the planetary alignment

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.430
is what allows the magic
inside the monument

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.370
to become active.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:06.790
To give himself time to produce

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.040
and distribute masks containing
specs from the monument,

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.920
he steals it nine months
ahead of Halloween

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.670
in January of 1982.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.300
The disappearance of
the Stonehenge monument

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.950
ends up being a mystery to the press.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.100
From the public's perspective,

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.730
it just disappears overnight.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:21.140
We don't know exactly how he
got such a massive artifact

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.340
out of England and into
the Western United States,

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.630
other than the fact that he
was aided by an army of robots

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.731
and still...

00:08:26.731 --> 00:08:28.497
- We had a time getting it here.

00:08:28.497 --> 00:08:31.050
- But we do know that his
evening lock-down of Santa Mira

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.560
probably made it easier to sneak

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.730
five tons of bluestone
back into his factory.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.130
As the season of the witch approached,

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:37.760
he used his profits from years and years

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.040
of successful entrepreneurship

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.450
to fund a massive TV and
radio marketing campaign,

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.283
ensuring that his masks

00:08:42.283 --> 00:08:44.973
would be the most popular
Halloween mask around kids.

00:08:44.973 --> 00:08:46.642
♪ Eight more days till Halloween ♪

00:08:46.642 --> 00:08:47.604
♪ Halloween ♪

00:08:47.604 --> 00:08:48.505
♪ Halloween ♪

00:08:48.505 --> 00:08:50.418
♪ Eight more days till Halloween ♪

00:08:50.418 --> 00:08:52.250
♪ Silver Shamrock ♪

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.910
There seems to even be something hypnotic

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:54.760
about the commercial,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.910
perhaps brainwashing them
into wanting these masks

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:57.970
more than any other.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.930
It seems that Cochran is
able to test the potency

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.380
of the microchips inside of his masks,

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.970
and their response to
the hypnotic commercial

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.500
by arranging several TV
monitors using the same layout

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.340
as the stones in the Stonehenge monument.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.340
When viewed from above,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.970
the spacing of each television monitor

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.630
mimics the formation of Stonehenge

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.100
and the tops of the television monitors

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.020
connect with the stone and start to glow.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.220
Throughout the course of the days

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.980
leading up to Halloween in 1982,

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.790
there is an advertisement
playing constantly

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.420
for the three Silver Shamrock masks

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.550
along with a big give away

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.450
that is supposedly going to
occur on TV on Halloween night.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.850
Everything goes according to plan

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.520
until Cochran comes across a
man named Harry Grimbridge.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.500
Harry was a shop owner local to California

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.880
who came to the factory to
pick up a new shipment of masks

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.450
in person on October 20th 1982.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.180
Cochran would often give his top sellers

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.250
tours of the factory,

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.390
perhaps to help incentivize high sales.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.500
Of course, he wouldn't show
them the most important part

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.670
of the mask making process,

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.420
what he calls final processing,

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.760
where the Stonehenge particle
microchip is implanted.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.380
It seems that at some
point during his tour,

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.370
Mr. Grimbridge discovered
what really goes on

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.340
in final processing,

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.400
and made it his goal to
warn the public about it,

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.550
so Cochran sends one of his
androids to hunt him down,

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.930
with instructions to kill Grimbridge

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.180
and then self-destructs.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.160
Of course this raises a lot of eyebrows

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.370
around the scene of the accident,

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.130
and eventually, on October 29th,

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.980
Mr. Grimbridge's doctor and his daughter

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:09.010
show up in Santa Mira looking for answers

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.963
about his untimely death.

00:10:10.963 --> 00:10:13.963
(suspenseful music)

00:10:16.076 --> 00:10:18.743
(ominous music)

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.780
They set themselves up at a local motel,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.110
not yet knowing that this was a part

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.750
of Cochran's area of influence.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.870
Seemingly everybody in
town is enamored with him,

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.470
as if he were someone like Walt Disney,

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:29.830
a sort of magical wonder.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.790
Others, like Marge
Guttman who is also there

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:32.623
to pick up a shipment,

00:10:32.623 --> 00:10:34.990
are annoyed with him and
his big business tactics.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.540
Cochran's plan for dealing with
the doctor, Daniel Challis,

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.950
and the daughter, Ellie Grimbridge,

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.800
is to essentially sweep
everything under the rug,

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.310
and pretend that Harry picked up his order

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:43.360
and went on his way.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.010
This is complicated, however,

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.070
when Marge Guttman gets
curious about the chip

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.410
she discovers on the back of
the Silver Shamrock trademark

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.830
attached to each mask, and
prods at it with a hairpin,

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.870
causing it to misfire,

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:54.490
blowing a hole through
her face with a laser

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:56.350
and causing bugs to come crawling out.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.000
He sends his androids
to clean up the mess,

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.140
and Cochran himself is
even forced to come out

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:02.000
and access the situation
in the middle of the night,

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.150
where he meets Ellie and
Challis for the first time.

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:05.460
He assures them that Ms. Guttman

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:06.690
is gonna be sent to the factory,

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.960
where they supposedly have
excellent medical facilities,

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.640
but Challis, being a doctor
himself, isn't really buying it.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.310
I mean why would a mask and toy factory

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.250
have its own hospital?

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.150
I mean, that's just asking for a lawsuit.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.320
This isn't a great excuse
from Cochran to be honest.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.350
And I think at this point,

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.840
he was just so close to Halloween,

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:21.800
and achieving his goal,

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.250
that he figured he
could tell them anything

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.410
and it would buy him enough time

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.990
to finish carrying out his plans.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.040
He even tries to act
hospitable the next day

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.290
when they show up at the factory,

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.860
by inviting Challis and Ellie along

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.960
as he gives another tour,

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.780
this time to Buddy Kupfer and
his family, a mask store owner

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:37.140
and the number one Silver
Shamrock salesman in the country.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.210
Before going on the tour,

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:41.420
Challis introduces himself and
Ellie as Mr. and Mrs. Smith,

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.130
which Cochran already knows is not true

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.670
because he's had an
eye on them for a while

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.940
and knows exactly who they
are and why they're here.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.700
He wants to send them
away peacefully though,

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.020
so he makes a big spectacle

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.730
by offering to replace Mr.
Grimbridge's lost order for free,

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.480
hoping to distract them
from the possibility

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.230
that his factory had anything
to do with Harry's death.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:01.123
- About the confusion over your order,

00:12:01.123 --> 00:12:02.570
I'll just tell you one thing.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.350
A replacement order is
being prepared for you

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.530
absolutely free, the whole thing's on me!

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.970
- He also has a big mural
of himself right behind him,

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.330
so between those two things,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:13.920
and the fact that he
basically made himself

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.210
the mayor of a town of robots,

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.250
the man seems to have
a pretty fragile ego.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.560
Perhaps he should have spent less time

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.210
congratulating himself and
more time hiding evidence,

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:22.470
because Ellie, at one point,

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.210
spots her father's car in plain sight

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.790
and immediately knows that this is where

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:26.880
he ran into trouble.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.760
Before they can get out of
town and sound the alarm,

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.790
he has some of his ro-boys kidnap Ellie.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.240
At this point, for reasons
that are still entirely unclear

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.540
to me, Cochran creates a
robot version of Ellie.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.530
I guess if I'm gonna try to
put a reasoning behind this,

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.880
he did this as a backup plan,

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.160
to maybe try to stop Challis

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.770
if he's somehow able to escape the town

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.150
and try to warn the public
about the Silver Shamrock masks?

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.560
In any event, it's pretty impressive

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.500
that he's able to create
a perfect robot replica

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.800
of her in just one day.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.460
He sends his bots after Challis too,

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.160
but he sneaks away out of their grasp

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.030
and goes to the factory
to try to save Ellie.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:55.720
Cochran quickly learns of the intrusion

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.120
and goes to find one of his androids

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.430
has been dismantled by Challis

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:01.100
and his knitting woman
animatronic decapitated.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:02.650
This time, when he sees his intruder,

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.150
he doesn't bother with entertaining

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:06.090
the false name that he gave last time.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.680
- Ah, Mr. Challis.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:08.653
- Where is Ellie?

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.700
- Mrs. Smith.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.460
- He takes Challis prisoner overnight.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.797
So the next day is Halloween,

00:13:13.797 --> 00:13:15.710
and Cochran takes a moment to appreciate

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.460
and breathe in that fresh autumn air.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.050
He knows that this is his big day.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.460
And he's about to gain an
immeasurable amount of power.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:24.000
He takes Challis down to
the final processing area.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.130
Now I know evil monologues

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:26.690
where the bad guy explains his entire plan

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.550
before it's too late for the
hero to do anything about it

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:29.640
are a common movie trope.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.590
Because the audience needs
to understand what's going on

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.830
and that's the easy way to do it,

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.150
so that's probably why he
essentially reveals everything

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.010
to Dr. Challis.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:38.410
But on the other hand, I'm
here to analyze his character,

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.220
so let's look at why he
might have done this.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:42.790
I imagine that the man
lived a very lonely life.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.690
He secludes himself up to a small town

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:45.720
in Northern California,

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.580
where he's surrounded entirely by robots

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:48.940
with very little personality.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:51.260
He's been alive for
probably thousands of years.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.820
All of his original friends and family

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.420
have most likely passed at this point,

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.510
and if any of them have
survived like he has,

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:58.500
I imagine that they're all
the way back in Ireland.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.190
Cochran seems to be a classic case

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.070
of the lonely at the top CEO.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.180
This probably explains
why he puts on the act

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:05.950
of being overly hospitable
when people come

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:06.850
to pick up orders,

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:08.910
and why he enjoys giving
tours of the factory.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.740
The man is starved for human interaction,

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.430
so he decides to get
the most out of Challis

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.070
before killing him, by
explaining his entire plan.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:17.420
That probably also explains
why he remains so friendly

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:20.000
with the man who's trying to
expose him, and take him down.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.670
He even shows Challis a
demonstration of the power bestowed

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.630
inside of each Silver
Shamrock Halloween masks

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.270
when the planets are aligned properly.

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:28.790
The Kupfer family, who he had
given the tour the day before,

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.150
is placed inside of a test room.

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:32.390
And a version of the Silver
Shamrock advert is played,

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.270
causing the young Kupfer boy to pass out

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.810
as his insides are turned into
a horde of crawling insects

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.070
and aggressive serpents.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.450
He leaves Challis tied up in
another test room that evening,

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:42.100
and places a mask over his face,

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.780
planning to let the
Silver Shamrock commercial

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.306
do the rest of the work.

00:14:45.306 --> 00:14:46.139
- And

00:14:48.977 --> 00:14:50.173
Happy Halloween.

00:14:50.173 --> 00:14:52.070
- Cochran goes back to his command center

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:52.970
at final processing,

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.710
where he makes a few
last minute phone calls,

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:56.270
and tells someone that
the Halloween giveaway

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.210
is just gonna be a fun
thank you for his customers,

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.890
when he's informed of a camera malfunction

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:00.870
in Challis's room.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:01.900
He sends his drones in,

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.740
where they discover that
their prisoner has escaped,

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:04.980
but he shows no concern,

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.690
because he's already got a plan B.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.920
He simply watches as Challis goes to save

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.410
what he thinks is Ellie,
but is actually robo-Ellie,

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.730
who is programmed to kill
him if he manages to escape.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.850
However, Dr. Challis doesn't
act as Cochran expected him to.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.080
Instead of leaving the factory,

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.140
he sneaks back into the
final processing room,

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:22.040
and starts playing the
commercial internally.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.520
He sees Challis scurrying away,

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.900
and sends his androids after him,

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.630
as he climbs up above the ceiling rafters,

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.900
where he dumps an entire
box full of mask trademarks

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.050
down onto the factory floor

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.360
while the commercial blasting through

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.540
the television monitors.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.110
This activates each of the buttons,

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:36.460
and the part of Stonehenge
residing in the factory.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.850
The interference causes all
of the robots in the area

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.750
to malfunction and fall to the ground.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.180
Yet still, Cochran doesn't seem concerned,

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:46.050
thrown off or even frustrated
at his plans being thwarted.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:48.120
In fact, he seems quite the opposite.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.980
He gives Challis a slow clap.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.890
As he does so, the stone zaps him

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.930
and he seemingly turns to stone himself,

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.950
which looks like either
something out of a nightmare

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.500
or something out of a hilarious meme,

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.490
then he completely disappears.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.900
He doesn't burn up or
turn into a swarm of bugs

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.920
like the victims that
we had previously seen.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:06.230
There's still some debate
as to what happened here.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.610
Did Cochran use the witchcraft
that he was so familiar with

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.360
to teleport himself out of the factory?

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:11.680
Or was the beam coming directly

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.230
from the Stonehenge monument itself

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:16.120
so powerful that it essentially
zapped him out of existence?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.540
Personally, I read this as
the death of Conal Cochran,

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.020
but to be honest, we'll probably
never find out for sure,

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:22.220
since it's been 40 years

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.800
with no more Halloween spin-off movies,

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.100
and the great Dan O'Herlihy,

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.910
who played Conal Cochran in
the film is no longer with us.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.320
That being said, I'd
definitely be in favor of them

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.460
making a movie called Halloween III 2,

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.080
so if you're watching this Universal,

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.010
let's make that happen.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.710
That will conclude today's lesson,

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:38.390
but let me know what
other Halloween characters

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.370
you'd like to see covered
here on Horror History.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:43.040
Subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week,

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:43.880
ring that deathbell

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.700
and make sure you select all notifications

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.520
and I'll see you in the next one.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.776
Assuming we both survive.

00:16:49.776 --> 00:16:52.359
(upbeat music)

